{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00264",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 5.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Doctor? Hi. I hope I've got the right time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.81,
      "end_seconds": 11.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.19,
      "end_seconds": 26.18,
      "duration_seconds": 13.99,
      "text": "Yeah, it's blood on the toilet paper. I don't know what's causing it. I've also had pain when I pass stool, for about two weeks. With pain when I pass stool, I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.61,
      "end_seconds": 29.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.11,
      "end_seconds": 34.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Uh, no problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.91,
      "end_seconds": 39.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Have you had any fever or change in bowel habit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.1,
      "end_seconds": 43.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "No, no fever or change in bowel habit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.93,
      "end_seconds": 49.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Any family history of bowel cancer or abdominal pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.87,
      "end_seconds": 56.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "I, I haven't had family history of bowel cancer or abdominal pain, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.65,
      "end_seconds": 63.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.59,
      "end_seconds": 75.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.03,
      "text": "Iron tablets. I take it once a day. I just want to get back to normal, really. Sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.75,
      "end_seconds": 79.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.98,
      "end_seconds": 85.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "About nearly five years. Anovate cream. I take it twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.96,
      "end_seconds": 91.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.92,
      "end_seconds": 103.97,
      "duration_seconds": 12.05,
      "text": "I mean, yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.3,
      "end_seconds": 110.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.59,
      "end_seconds": 139.65,
      "duration_seconds": 28.06,
      "text": "I have low haemoglobin. I didn't want to make a fuss, uh, you know. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. Yes, migraines. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am. Hmm, um, yes, heart disease. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.92,
      "end_seconds": 150.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.72,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the low haemoglobin in your file as well. Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.12,
      "end_seconds": 155.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Um, just a bypass operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.24,
      "end_seconds": 159.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.55,
      "end_seconds": 160.33,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.35,
      "end_seconds": 177.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.29,
      "end_seconds": 182.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "Well, um, my father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.05,
      "end_seconds": 188.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.63,
      "end_seconds": 193.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Ibuprofen. I come out in... well, stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.7,
      "end_seconds": 195.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.15,
      "end_seconds": 208.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.19,
      "end_seconds": 227.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 111 over 71, SpO2 99 percent on room air, heart rate 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.65,
      "end_seconds": 230.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.95,
      "end_seconds": 235.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.21,
      "end_seconds": 241.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.43,
      "end_seconds": 243.13,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.09,
      "end_seconds": 247.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.19,
      "end_seconds": 262.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Tummy is soft and non-tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 263.06,
      "end_seconds": 263.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.7,
      "end_seconds": 286.92,
      "duration_seconds": 17.22,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like haemorrhoids. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be something higher up in the bowel that we shouldn't miss, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.91,
      "end_seconds": 294.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, you know, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.01,
      "end_seconds": 311.23,
      "duration_seconds": 15.22,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's haemorrhoids, and we'll know more once the a colonoscopy is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had blood on the toilet paper, and no family history of bowel cancer or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.92,
      "end_seconds": 314.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "That's it, you know, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.77,
      "end_seconds": 342.7,
      "duration_seconds": 26.93,
      "text": "We should do a colonoscopy for rectal bleeding. Let's get blood tests, for rectal bleeding. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm prescribing a soothing cream, twice a day, for one week. That's for haemorrhoids. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Let's use lactulose, 15 ml, at night, for two weeks. It's for constipation."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.16,
      "end_seconds": 347.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Okay, um, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.5,
      "end_seconds": 367.59,
      "duration_seconds": 19.09,
      "text": "Soak in a warm bath for ten minutes after you pass stool, and don't strain. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. Keep an eye out, and if you pass a lot of blood or feel faint, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.45,
      "end_seconds": 369.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.18,
      "end_seconds": 379.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Please come and see me in three weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.2,
      "end_seconds": 386.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "So, I take the lactulose, 15 ml, at night. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.19,
      "end_seconds": 392.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.94,
      "end_seconds": 397.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I mean, um, no questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.69,
      "end_seconds": 400.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}